{
  // The unit suite's own typecheck (issue #942). `tsconfig.json` is the BUILD
  // config — `rootDir: "src"`, `composite`, emits to `dist` — so it can never
  // include `tests/**`. That is how 41k lines of test code reached August 2026
  // without a compiler ever looking at them, and why #838 could sit there: six
  // tests died on a bare `TypeError` from fixtures that were not valid
  // `Recipe`s, with nothing to say so. Wired into the root `typecheck` script
  // beside `e2e/tsconfig.json` and the CF probes.
  //
  // `src` is in scope alongside `tests` for two reasons: `src/env.d.ts` carries
  // the `*.svelte` module shim and the `ImportMetaEnv` shape, and a test's props
  // are only checked against the thing under test when both are in one program.
  // Note the limit of that shim — it types every component as a bare
  // `Component`, so what a test passes as PROPS is not checked here. Prop
  // checking needs `svelte-check`, which is a separate (larger) job.
  //
  // `scripts/**` joined in #1132, the same hole one directory along: the build
  // config is `rootDir: "src"` and `e2e/tsconfig.json` covers `e2e/**`, so this
  // app's two `node --experimental-strip-types` scripts were named by NO program
  // in the root `typecheck` script. ESLint parsed them syntactically and nothing
  // else looked — which is how `process-e2e-coverage.ts` came to be the
  // unexercised half of #945's "the collection code is untouched and still
  // here". They belong in a test program rather than the build one for the
  // reason `tests/**` does: they never emit and `src` never imports them.
  // Note the limit — `tsc` checks types, not whether Node's type STRIPPER can
  // run the file (`erasableSyntaxOnly` is deliberately not set here; it would
  // bind `src` and `tests` too, which is a wider question than this app's two
  // scripts). What proves the stripper still runs `process-e2e-coverage.ts` is
  // `tests/e2eCoverageReport.test.ts`, which spawns the real interpreter.
  // `generate-icons.ts` has no such test and is only type-checked.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": ".",
    "composite": false,
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "tests/**/*", "scripts/**/*"]
}
